WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:07.600
“I would like to here again state that 106
is not, as is commonly believed, a basic predator,

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.610
on par with an advanced shark.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:15.449
SCP-106 is a sentient being, albeit a totally
alien one.

00:00:15.449 --> 00:00:20.580
SCP-106 appears to be aware of several things
beyond the scope of pure instinct and genetic

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:21.760
memory.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:27.650
SCP-106 consistently breaches at moments where
recovery and containment are most difficult.

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:32.680
A fox may see his way out of a trap, but only
a man will wait for his captors to look away

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:33.680
to escape.”

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.440
-Dr. Allok, from his paper, On Sentience In
Contained Humanoids

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.870
They say that patience is a virtue.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:47.399
If this is true, it’s the only virtue that
SCP-106 has in spades.

00:00:47.399 --> 00:00:52.460
The anomaly known as the Old Man had been
well-behaved for months, sitting cross-legged

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:58.360
in the center of his containment chamber,
his lipless mouth molded into a slight grin.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:05.990
The Old Man had a reptilian-like calm to him:
Never truly inactive, just waiting.

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:09.510
And nobody else can wait for quite as long
as him.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:14.130
He could go for years without so much as twitching
if he wanted to.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:15.610
But not today.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:17.820
Today was special.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:24.160
There were no clocks and no calendars in SCP-106’s
cell, but that was fine.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:30.890
He remembered the last day they locked him
back up, and he’d been counting ever since.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:39.110
Seconds, minutes, days, months...The Old Man
had all the time in the world, and today,

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:41.450
it was all about to pay off.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:43.270
October 31st.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:44.990
All Hallow’s Eve.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:49.640
The night when ghosts, goblins, and demons
come out to play.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:52.640
The Old Man almost chuckled at the thought
of it.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:56.119
What a perfect day for a containment breach…

00:01:56.119 --> 00:02:01.000
One of the Foundation Technicians observing
106 from a control room monitor spilled his

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:05.140
coffee when the Old Man got up and started
walking towards the wall.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:09.979
Alarms went off and guards were dispatched
as a large, dark stain expanded on the wall

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:14.730
of the containment chamber, and 106 walked
through it.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:18.260
Not that any amount of armed response would
do them any good.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:23.950
The bullets passed right through 106’s inky
flesh as he strolled down the corridor towards

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.099
the exit.

00:02:25.099 --> 00:02:29.349
He killed two guards and a researcher on his
way out, just for the fun of it.

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:34.010
He’d been a well-behaved creature for a
long time now - he’d earned an evening of

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.980
letting his purely-metaphorical hair down.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:44.599
And when SCP-106 decides to have a night of
good fun, horror is always sure to follow.

00:02:44.599 --> 00:02:50.750
This is the tale of one of SCP-106’s most
infamous and horrifying containment breaches.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:54.320
Be warned: The following isn’t for the faint
of heart.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:03:00.990
You’re about to learn why SCP-106 is still
one of the most feared anomalies in Foundation

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:01.990
containment.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:06.860
Immediately, the containment site dispatched
three of its best field agents: Agent Park,

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:08.920
Agent Weng, and Agent Drak.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:15.760
Their task was simple: Locate SCP-106, minimize
potential casualties, and distract the sadistic

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.349
anomaly long enough for reinforcements to
come and contain the creature once again.

00:03:20.349 --> 00:03:26.590
For the last several years, these agents would
eat, sleep, and breathe all things 106 in

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.820
preparation for a moment just like this.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:33.349
They’d been drilled over and over again
on everything from the creature’s behavior,

00:03:33.349 --> 00:03:37.989
to the worst case scenario of what to do if
you get pulled into its nightmarish pocket

00:03:37.989 --> 00:03:38.989
dimension.

00:03:38.989 --> 00:03:43.810
They were as trained as a person possibly
could be for this situation and fitted with

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:46.780
state of the art Foundation equipment to boot.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.569
And yet, they were still terrified.

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:54.209
They passed through the streets of the nearest
city, where containment experts believed 106

00:03:54.209 --> 00:03:57.099
was most likely to head after his escape.

00:03:57.099 --> 00:04:01.960
People of all ages, dressed in Halloween costumes
were out enjoying the night.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:06.290
Child sized super heroes were hanging out
with even smaller villains.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:10.090
Horror movie slashers were sharing drinks
with cops and nuns.

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:13.480
Countless candy-carrying zombies wandered
through the streets.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:18.569
None of them had any idea of the true horror
that walked among them.

00:04:18.569 --> 00:04:22.079
The three agents went over their training
silently in their minds.

00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:26.860
106 was intelligent - more intelligent than
anyone back at the Foundation really gave

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:28.090
it credit for.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:32.710
It’d planned this; it knew that it could
blend in among the costumed monsters that

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.780
were sure to be out tonight.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:38.849
Nobody would be able to tell the difference
until it was too late…

00:04:38.849 --> 00:04:42.460
One such person was a young woman named Alice.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:47.430
Dressed up as an angel, her experience that
night would be far from heaven-sent.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:51.569
Her boyfriend had made the always classy move
of breaking up with her right before they

00:04:51.569 --> 00:04:56.770
were supposed to head to a Halloween party,
leaving her in a fit of emotional distress

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.199
and embarrassment.

00:04:58.199 --> 00:05:02.550
Over the course of the next several hours,
she obsessively reflected on her ex-boyfriend’s

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:09.319
audacity and lack of empathy toward her, burdening
her mind and filling her head with anxiety.

00:05:09.319 --> 00:05:14.949
His last words, “I’m sorry, it’s over!”
gradually became louder and louder in her

00:05:14.949 --> 00:05:19.520
thoughts, as she stumbled in sadness away
from the noise of the streets towards a thicket

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:20.650
of trees.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:26.270
She was in such despair she could barely stand,
and as she staggered through the vegetation,

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:30.560
she didn’t even notice the shuffling of
footsteps behind her, or that they were getting

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:34.360
closer and closer and closer…

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:37.330
Alice tripped, and caught herself against
a nearby tree.

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:41.979
That’s when she noticed a sudden burning
sensation on the skin of her hand.

00:05:41.979 --> 00:05:47.139
She looked up and saw that her hand was now
coated in a sticky, tar-like substance.

00:05:47.139 --> 00:05:51.949
Whatever it was, it seemed to be eating away
at the tree, and she could hear the hiss of

00:05:51.949 --> 00:05:55.589
the corrosive liquid as it melted the skin
of her hand.

00:05:55.589 --> 00:06:00.120
A twig cracked behind her and she turned to
see the rotting Old Man staring at her with

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:01.960
a malicious grin.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:07.249
She screamed, and began to run, but the alcohol
had robbed her of her coordination.

00:06:07.249 --> 00:06:12.169
She tried as hard as she could to escape while
cradling her burning hand, but it wasn’t

00:06:12.169 --> 00:06:13.169
enough.

00:06:13.169 --> 00:06:17.050
She felt a spike of excruciating pain rock
her nervous system.

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:21.419
The Old Man had reached into her back, like
a man operating a puppet.

00:06:21.419 --> 00:06:27.509
His long, burning fingers, dripping with corrosive
grease, had melted through her skin, and grabbed

00:06:27.509 --> 00:06:29.189
her by the spine.

00:06:29.189 --> 00:06:32.949
She screamed in pain, but she was too far
away.

00:06:32.949 --> 00:06:34.689
Not a soul could hear her.

00:06:34.689 --> 00:06:40.330
And the only creature that could didn’t
have anything resembling a soul.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:44.259
The creature grabbed her, and pulled her into
its blistering embrace.

00:06:44.259 --> 00:06:49.050
It smiled the whole time, baring every rotten
tooth.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:53.439
It held her in place, burning the rest of
her body as the two of them sank into the

00:06:53.439 --> 00:06:57.689
ground together, more acidic sludge pooling
at their feet.

00:06:57.689 --> 00:07:03.119
Alice screamed on, and SCP-106 loved her all
the more for it.

00:07:03.119 --> 00:07:06.080
The screamers were its favorite.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:10.819
By the time Agent Drak, Parks, and Weng found
Alice, it was hard to know that this had once

00:07:10.819 --> 00:07:12.149
been a human.

00:07:12.149 --> 00:07:16.069
But they knew one thing for certain: that
this was the work of the Old Man.

00:07:16.069 --> 00:07:21.340
And they suspected that he wasn’t close
to being done with his campaign of Halloween

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:22.340
terror.

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:26.430
Next, came a little boy named Jason and his
unfortunate friends.

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:31.249
They were dressed as the Justice League, with
Jason leading the group as Batman, all of

00:07:31.249 --> 00:07:34.699
them wearing costumes that made them feel
like true heroes.

00:07:34.699 --> 00:07:38.669
It’d been a good night, their bags heavy
with candy.

00:07:38.669 --> 00:07:42.469
As they walked down an alleyway they’d passed
through countless times on their way home

00:07:42.469 --> 00:07:46.560
from school, they had no idea what was waiting
for them.

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:51.639
A long, gnarled hand, dripping with black
ooze, suddenly shot out of the wall and grabbed

00:07:51.639 --> 00:07:53.770
the boy dressed as Superman.

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:58.800
He screamed as he was pulled towards the ooze,
his braces shining in the moonlight, and kept

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.749
screaming until he disappeared into the solid
brick wall.

00:08:02.749 --> 00:08:07.059
The rest of the “Justice League” broke
into frightened screams and scattered.

00:08:07.059 --> 00:08:09.309
But they weren’t fast enough.

00:08:09.309 --> 00:08:13.869
Hands kept emerging from the wall, grabbing
the children, burning them, pulling them into

00:08:13.869 --> 00:08:15.240
the dark.

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:20.599
Only Jason got away, running and screaming
as his friends were yanked into the void.

00:08:20.599 --> 00:08:24.309
But no one gets away from the Old Man that
easily.

00:08:24.309 --> 00:08:29.740
A black puddle formed on the ground in front
of Jason, and the Old Man rose out of it,

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:32.709
still grinning its malicious, spiteful grin.

00:08:32.709 --> 00:08:36.310
Jason fell to the ground, his legs giving
out from the fear.

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:42.819
But the Old Man didn’t move, he just stared
at him, sizing him up, deciding what type

00:08:42.819 --> 00:08:46.079
of torment would yield the most twisted pleasure.

00:08:46.079 --> 00:08:50.300
The creature lifted something up to its mouth,
something that might have been mistaken for

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:53.340
a piece of Halloween candy from a distance.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:54.880
But Jason knew better.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:09:00.680
It was a tooth, and Jason could recognize
the shining braces still stuck to it.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:06.339
The Old Man put the tooth in his mouth, and
crunched it like a jawbreaker, as Jason almost

00:09:06.339 --> 00:09:09.410
passed out from the sheer terror of watch
it.

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:12.649
To this day, nobody knows why the Old Man
spared Jason.

00:09:12.649 --> 00:09:17.860
But when Agents Drak, Parks, and Weng found
the boy, the only survivor from the massacre

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:22.430
of his friends, he was gripping the metal
fragment from Billy’s tooth so hard that

00:09:22.430 --> 00:09:24.630
it was embedded into his palm.

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:26.800
But the night still wasn’t over yet.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:32.290
The Old Man still wanted to have just a little
bit more Halloween fun.

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:36.860
One little boy couldn’t join in on the Halloween
adventures all his friends were having.

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:41.250
He was stuck at home, sick with a stomach
flu that had been going around at school.

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:46.680
All he could do was sit and watch scary movies
as his mother answered the door, passing out

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:49.769
candy to the trick or treaters that he wished
he could join.

00:09:49.769 --> 00:09:54.900
He sighed as he heard his mom at the front
door giving candy to pirates, zombies, and

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:56.060
vampires.

00:09:56.060 --> 00:10:00.440
Tomorrow would be even worse when he was forced
to watch his friends eating their candy and

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:04.220
reminiscing about all the fun he wasn’t
involved in.

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:07.850
His self-pitying was interrupted though when
he heard his mother open the door to another

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:08.880
trick or treater.

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:13.649
But this time, there was no exchange of words
or candy.

00:10:13.649 --> 00:10:17.079
Just a long, blood-curdling scream.

00:10:17.079 --> 00:10:21.630
The little boy quickly got up to investigate,
his heart pounding in his chest.

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:26.560
The sounds of his mother’s pain kept echoing
down the hall, as the heavy footsteps of something

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.140
else approached.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:34.291
It rounded the corner, and the little boy
saw it, in all of its horrifying glory, like

00:10:34.291 --> 00:10:39.170
something out of one of the horror movies
he had been watching, only worse.

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:44.870
It was the rotting Old Man, dragging his dying
mother along with one hand that was stuck

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:49.490
right into the flesh of her chest and grabbing
her by the ribcage.

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:54.620
He screamed and ran upstairs towards the bathroom,
the only room in the house with a lock.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:59.180
He could hear the plodding footsteps of the
creature following him up the stairs followed

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:04.710
by the sickening sound of what must have been
the Old Man dropping his mother’s body.

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:09.560
The little boy slammed the bathroom door shut,
locked it, and collapsed against the wood.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:14.410
His face was hot and sticky with tears, but
at least he was safe for the moment.

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:18.290
Surely someone had heard his mother’s screams
and would come to save him.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:22.790
As he was imagining the police bursting through
the front door and gunning down the monster,

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:25.569
he heard a hissing sound coming from above
him.

00:11:25.569 --> 00:11:30.600
He looked up, and saw the face of the Old
Man, melting through the door and smiling

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:32.310
at him from above.

00:11:32.310 --> 00:11:37.100
He tried to scream but the monster opened
its mouth and a tide of corrosive liquid hit

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:38.900
him in the face.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:43.291
Moments later, someone did burst through the
front door, but it wasn’t the police, it

00:11:43.291 --> 00:11:48.040
was the three agents, drawn to the Old Man’s
location by a trail of violence and acidic

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.639
black mucus.

00:11:49.639 --> 00:11:55.260
And as far as 106 was concerned, this was
a great thing - he’d just finished breaking

00:11:55.260 --> 00:12:00.939
his last set of toys, and the new ones were
here right on schedule.

00:12:00.939 --> 00:12:04.730
Parks fired at the creature, but it wasn’t
enough to save Agent Drak.

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:10.199
He was standing just a little too close, and
underestimated how fast the creature could

00:12:10.199 --> 00:12:11.199
move.

00:12:11.199 --> 00:12:15.649
Before he knew it, he was being dragged into
a messy portal in the wall by an entity that

00:12:15.649 --> 00:12:18.459
was beyond his darkest nightmares.

00:12:18.459 --> 00:12:24.211
When he woke up, he was in the one place that
anyone who knows about SCP-106 hopes never

00:12:24.211 --> 00:12:30.569
to find themselves: The Pocket Dimension,
that labyrinth of twisting, rotting hallways

00:12:30.569 --> 00:12:33.060
where the Old Man has total dominion.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:38.820
You’d rather be in Hell, under the care
of the devil himself than end up there.

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:43.769
Agent Drak encountered horrors beyond conception
before he finally, mercifully, died at the

00:12:43.769 --> 00:12:45.610
Old Man’s hands.

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:50.319
No weapons or training could save him, no
amount of effort could dig him out of this

00:12:50.319 --> 00:12:51.319
hole.

00:12:51.319 --> 00:12:57.459
He ran through the halls for four whole days
before SCP-106 finally got bored, and started

00:12:57.459 --> 00:13:04.420
taking him apart, but to Agent Drak, those
four days felt like a wretched eternity.

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:09.730
When they eventually found SCP-106, he was
standing in a field, stomping on pumpkins

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:10.920
out of boredom.

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:15.830
He submitted to containment with relatively
little difficulty, as Foundation field agents

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:18.470
used high-intensity lights to subdue him.

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:22.529
Clean up crews applied amnestics and generated
cover stories.

00:13:22.529 --> 00:13:26.249
Everything about the Halloween night massacre
was swept under the rug.

00:13:26.249 --> 00:13:32.589
Back in containment, SCP-106 once again sat
cross-legged on the floor of his cell, sorting

00:13:32.589 --> 00:13:36.069
a little collection of its victim’s teeth
like Halloween candy.

00:13:36.069 --> 00:13:41.740
He sat and smiled, mulling over the memories
of his delightful halloween night.

00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:46.779
He’d be fine for another few months now,
he could just sit and enjoy the thoughts until

00:13:46.779 --> 00:13:50.680
the Foundation got bored and loosened the
leash again.

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:53.040
106 is a patient monster.

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:56.089
When the time came, he’d be ready.

00:13:56.089 --> 00:13:58.009
He was always ready.

00:13:58.009 --> 00:14:04.899
Now go check out “SCP-001 - When Day Breaks”
and “SCP-3280 - After the Storm” for more

00:14:04.899 --> 00:14:07.700
terrifying tales from the SCP Foundation!

